---
import '../../styles/framework.css';
import OutlineIcon from '../shared/OutlineIcon.astro';
---

<section id="framework" class="framework-section section-pad">
  <div class="container framework-shell">
    <div class="section-copy framework-copy">
      <div class="framework-heading">
        <figure class="framework-portrait">
          <img src="/images/women-four-signals.webp" alt="Parent reflecting on stream choices and future direction" loading="lazy" width="220" height="220" />
        </figure>
        <div class="framework-heading-copy">
          <div class="framework-kicker">
            <OutlineIcon name="sparkles" size={16} />
            <p class="label muted">Core mechanism</p>
          </div>
          <h2>Four signals are stronger than one marksheet.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        In the webinar, we show parents how stream decisions should be evaluated using four practical signals that are
        more reliable than marks alone.
      </p>
      <p class="framework-close">Marks matter. But marks alone are not enough.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar-grid" aria-label="Four assessment pillars">
      <article class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-kicker">
          <span class="pillar-icon"><OutlineIcon name="brain" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="pillar-label">Aptitude</span>
        </div>
        <h3>What comes naturally</h3>
        <p>Spot whether your child naturally leans toward analytical problem-solving, pattern recognition, or subject depth before pressure takes over.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-kicker">
          <span class="pillar-icon"><OutlineIcon name="compass" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="pillar-label">Personality</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Environment and fit</h3>
        <p>Understand whether your child performs better with structure, independence, pace, collaboration, or lower-pressure learning environments.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-kicker">
          <span class="pillar-icon"><OutlineIcon name="sparkles" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="pillar-label">Interests</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Sustained curiosity</h3>
        <p>Separate genuine long-term interest from imitation, peer influence, or temporary excitement about a popular path.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-kicker">
          <span class="pillar-icon"><OutlineIcon name="book-open" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="pillar-label">Study style</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Execution habits</h3>
        <p>See how your child handles logic, memorisation, revision, focus, and self-driven work so stream choices feel more realistic.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
